# The external-test profile: middleware overrides.
#
# Layered ON TOP of telecom-middleware/.env by start-testable.ps1 - it changes only the
# four things that stop an outside runner from reaching the service, and inherits the
# store, the seed and everything else from your real local configuration.
#
# Why each line is here:

# TestSprite runs from its own cloud, so the port has to be reachable off-box. The
# tunnel forwards to this.
TELECOM_MW_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0

# The runner injects ONE header set - Authorization - and this API wants two
# credentials. With SERVICE_AUTH=jwks every call is refused at the door before any
# route logic runs, which is exactly what the last report showed: six blocked tests,
# all 401 service_not_recognised, none of them about the code under test.
#
# 'unchecked' is safe here and nowhere else: the settings validator refuses it when
# TELECOM_MW_ENV=production, and app.py logs a warning every start while it is set on
# a non-loopback interface. Take the tunnel down when you are done.
TELECOM_MW_SERVICE_AUTH=unchecked

# A token minted by telecom-mcp/scripts/mint_dev_token.py is HS256. Verifier 'jwks'
# would reject it as token_invalid - the second report's ten failures in one line.
# Both services must agree, so this is set in both override files.
TELECOM_MW_IDENTITY_VERIFIER=local

# Real Auth0 is the production path and is not what an external smoke test needs.
# Nothing below is required while IDENTITY_VERIFIER=local, but the audience is: the
# minted token carries it, and the verifier checks it.
TELECOM_MW_JWT_AUDIENCE=https://api.telecom.example/v1
